WEBVTT

00:00:58.219 --> 00:01:00.987
and see it as a sign of poverty.

00:01:01.524 --> 00:01:03.150
And I disagree.

00:01:03.174 --> 00:01:05.624
In fact, I think there's
a lot we can learn

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:07.783
from ancient Mongolian nomads

00:01:07.807 --> 00:01:09.030
that will help us survive

00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:11.534
in the years and decades to come.

00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:17.901
This is a picture of me playing Mongolia's
most celebrated traditional instrument,

00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:19.266
morin khuur,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.705
or horsehead fiddle.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:24.963
I started playing the instrument
when I was only nine,

00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:27.916
and by 11 I was traveling the world

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.934
representing Mongolia
at international festivals,